Make upstream's systemVerify safe on older macOS: the SSL policy is passed as a
single SecPolicyRef rather than inside a one-element CFArray (on OS X 10.9,
SecTrustEvaluate faults when the policies argument is an array built by
CFArrayCreateMutable, which has no retain callbacks), and below 10.15 the
evaluation and chain use SecTrustEvaluate and SecTrustGetCertificateAtIndex,
the chain loop adapted from Go 1.24's
(https://github.com/golang/go/blob/go1.24.13/src/crypto/x509/root_darwin.go).
10.15+ keeps upstream's calls.

Through Go 1.26 this patch also replaced darwin's loadSystemRoots here. Go 1.27
moved loadSystemRoots into the shared root.go, so the keychain union is served
from there now (patch 0016, root_keychainunion_darwin.go's
keychainUnionPlatformRoots).

